1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bxd7+ Qxd7 5. c4 Nc6 6. d4 cxd4 7. Nxd4 g6 8. Nc3 Bg7 9. Be3 Nf6 10. h3 O-O 11. O-O Rac8 12. b3 Rfd8 13. Rc1 e6 14. f4 d5 15. cxd5 exd5 16. e5 Ne8 17. Na4 Qe7 $2 (17... b6 18. Qd2 Nxd4 19. Qxd4 Rxc1 20. Rxc1 Nc7 21. Rd1 Ne6 22. Qd2 d4 23. Bf2 Bh6 24. g3 Nxf4 $5 25. gxf4 Qxh3 26. Nb2 Qg4+ 27. Kf1 Bxf4 {with good chances}) 18. Qd2 Nxd4 19. Qxd4 b6 20. Rxc8 Rxc8 21. Qxd5 Rd8 22. Qc4 Qd7 23. Nc3 Qd3 24. Qxd3 Rxd3 25. Nd1 Nc7 26. Kf2 f6 27. Ke2 Rd7 28. exf6 Bxf6 29. Nf2 Re7 30. Rd1 Nb5 31. Kf3 Kf7 32. Rd3 Nc3 33. a4 Ke6 34. Ne4 Nxe4 35. Kxe4 Rc7 36. g4 Rg7 37. f5+ gxf5+ 38. gxf5+ Ke7 39. Bf4 Rg2 40. Bd6+ Kf7 41. Bb8 Re2+ 42. Kd5 Re7 43. Kc6 Be5 44. Bxe5 Rxe5 45. Rd7+ Kf6 46. Rxa7 h5 47. Kxb6 Re3 48. b4 Rxh3 49. a5 Kxf5 50. a6 Ra3 51. Rh7 {Source: "Forever a 180" by Oliver Jackson (self-published) via Nigel Short. N.b. there are conflicting reports as to whether this tournament was held on the 7-9 July or 14-16 July - I'm plumping for the latter but I'm not certain - JS} 1-0

