1. e4 c6 2. Ne2 g6 3. d4 Bg7 4. Nbc3 d5 5. e5 f6 $1 6. Bf4 Nd7 $1 7. exf6 Ngxf6 8. h3 O-O 9. g4 Qe8 $1 10. Bg2 e5 11. dxe5 Nxe5 12. O-O h5 $3 {The best move in the game!} 13. g5 Nh7 (13... Ne4 $2 14. Nxd5 $1) 14. Kh1 Qe7 15. Bh2 $1 {A clever move that deserved a better fate; Nigel exploits the possible fork by f4 and tempts me into the unclear line. 15...f3!? 16 f4! etc..} Nf7 {A strange-looking move, but the knight is heading via d6 to f5, given the chance.} 16. h4 Qb4 $1 {planning after 17 f4 g4! followed by ...d6-f5 with a strategically won game. This tempts Nigel into a desperate sacrifice which looks more dangerous than it is.} 17. Bxd5 $6 cxd5 18. Nxd5 Qc5 $1 ({But not the obvious} 18... Qe4+ 19. f3 {when Black is in trouble.}) 19. b4 Qc6 20. f3 Re8 21. Nef4 Bf5 22. b5 Qc4 $1 {Source: John Littlewood via Keith Brown} ({The game might end} 22... Qc4 23. Rc1 Rad8 {ties White up completely.}) 0-1

